e: Web Search\n---\nNOTE: The NAEP Mathematics scale ranges from <strong>0 to 500</strong>.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"be2a5451962f6de9\">>>", "siteName": "www.fldoe.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"84a3f9e0e238ca39\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT NATION  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"84a3f9e0e238ca39\">>>", "url": "https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011NP8.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a789744c053af86d\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNOTE: The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from <strong>0 to 500</strong>. Results presented in this report are based on public school students only.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a789744c053af86d\">>>", "siteName": "nces.ed.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e5c9bc928107173d\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP State and District Snapshots\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e5c9bc928107173d\">>>", "url": "https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/snapshots/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"50ea558dd6b7f9fb\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nExplore and download state and district snapshots of NAEP data in mathematics, reading, science, and writing.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"50ea558dd6b7f9fb\">>>", "siteName": "nces.ed.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e6a3c24188b9e9d6\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT KANSAS  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e6a3c24188b9e9d6\">>>", "url": "https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011KS8.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a0fb74ccd35bf440\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNOTE: The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from <strong>0 to 500</strong>. Results presented in this report are based on public school students only.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a0fb74ccd35bf440\">>>", "siteName": "nces.ed.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"27e15589283f8dbd\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Mathematics: State Student Group Scores\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"27e15589283f8dbd\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/groups/?grade=8", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9941f711b53bb864\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nWhile average scores decreased between 2019 and 2022 for almost all student groups nationally, this overall pattern differed across the states. Compared to 2019, female students scored lower in 38 states in 2022, whereas male fourth-graders scored lower in 26 states.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9941f711b53bb864\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8031f74d61a21d49\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2022 NAEP Mathematics Assessment: Highlighted Results at Grades 4 and 8 for the Nation, States, and Districts | IES\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8031f74d61a21d49\">>>", "url": "https://nces.ed.gov/use-work/resource-library/report/statistical-analysis-report/2022-naep-mathematics-assessment-highlighted-results-grades-4-and-8-nation-states-and-districts", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"57d0f5fdb4544180\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThis report presents selected results from the National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP) 2022 mathematics assessment. The report includes national, state, and district results on the performance of fourth- and eighth-grade students. Results are presented in terms of average scores and as percentages of students performing at or above the three NAEP achievement levels: NAEP Basic, NAEP Proficient, and NAEP Advanced.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"57d0f5fdb4544180\">>>", "siteName": "nces.ed.gov"}]}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1775299852029}}
