 Web Search\n---\nNOVEMBER 2022\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"69154253a72906bf\">>>", "url": "https://csgsouth.org/wp-content/uploads/QofM-November.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a74ee82867c37c9e\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nOn October 24, 2022, the United States Department of Education’s National Center for Education Statistics (NCES) released the results of the National Assessment of Education Progress (NAEP) – commonly referred to as “The Nation’s · Report Card.” Due to the pandemic’s impact, the national average scores in mathematics for fourth- and eighth-graders\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a74ee82867c37c9e\">>>", "siteName": "csgsouth.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"82d4f0208710e6f6\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2024 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT KENTUCKY  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"82d4f0208710e6f6\">>>", "url": "https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2024/pdf/2024219KY8.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"33a87fd1c497c179\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nAVERAGE SCORES FOR STATE/JURISDICTION ... performance gap was not significantly different from that in 2000 ... NOTE: The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from <strong>0 to 500</strong>....\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"33a87fd1c497c179\">>>", "siteName": "nces.ed.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"99b183c9c0f40a75\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2024 Mathematics Snapshot Report for Kentucky Grade 8\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"99b183c9c0f40a75\">>>", "url": "https://www.education.ky.gov/AA/Reports/Documents/snapshot_MAT2024KY_8.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6144fc05e064c93c\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nAn Official Website of the Commonwealth of Kentucky · Kentucky’s United We Learn Vision for education in Kentucky consists of three big ideas​​\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6144fc05e064c93c\">>>", "siteName": "www.education.ky.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b76bb48111b544bb\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nKentucky Shows Promise with Post-COVID Test Scores – Prichard Committee for Academic Excellence\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b76bb48111b544bb\">>>", "url": "https://prichardcommittee.org/kentucky-shows-promise-with-post-covid-test-scores/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"75d517edafdc5c85\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nIn percent of students reaching NAEP proficiency or above, Kentucky’s newest results are statistically tied with the nation in grade 4 reading, grade 8 reading and grade 4 math, with results below the nation in grade 8 math. Kentucky’s 4th-grade math results showed statistically significant improvement compared to 2022.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"75d517edafdc5c85\">>>", "published": "January 29, 2025", "siteName": "prichardcommittee.org"}]}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1775299857660}}
