 only.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"dfe471fa4ce3ded5\">>>", "siteName": "nces.ed.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"73d0f21325135629\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nAverage National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP) mathematics scale score of 8th-grade public school students, by state or jurisdiction: Selected years, 1990 through 2022\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"73d0f21325135629\">>>", "url": "https://nces.ed.gov/programs/digest/d22/tables/dt22_222.60.asp", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f44ff205a1ccf265\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nPrevious Page Download Excel (52KB)\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f44ff205a1ccf265\">>>", "siteName": "nces.ed.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8f6ee9f1dd54b50a\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Mathematics: State Student Group Scores\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8f6ee9f1dd54b50a\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/groups/?grade=8", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c27b6b92a6e3dad8\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nWhile average scores decreased between 2019 and 2022 for almost all student groups nationally, this overall pattern differed across the states. Compared to 2019, female students scored lower in 38 states in 2022, whereas male fourth-graders scored lower in 26 states.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c27b6b92a6e3dad8\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ad13752ee699d79d\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP scores by state - Ballotpedia\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ad13752ee699d79d\">>>", "url": "https://ballotpedia.org/NAEP_scores_by_state", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"4ebf5e027a8cfa10\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe table below details math and reading scores for students in fourth grade and eighth grade using the National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP). All 50 states and Washington, D.C.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"4ebf5e027a8cfa10\">>>", "siteName": "ballotpedia.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"35abe4210edd3efe\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nExplore Results for the 2022 NAEP Mathematics Assessment\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"35abe4210edd3efe\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/?grade=8", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c06cdc14cc630752\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nDownload a summary of the 2022 mathematics results. ... More detailed mathematics assessment results are available throughout this Report Card. ... The NAEP mathematics assessment measures students&#x27; knowledge and skills in mathematics and students&#x27; ability to apply their knowledge in problem-solving situations.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c06cdc14cc630752\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}]}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1775299904510}}
