 "siteName": "nces.ed.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1a05b81cd39b15e8\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP scores by state - Ballotpedia\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1a05b81cd39b15e8\">>>", "url": "https://ballotpedia.org/NAEP_scores_by_state", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"caf2b68a3fae283f\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe table below details math and reading scores for students in fourth grade and eighth grade using the National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP). All 50 states and Washington, D.C.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"caf2b68a3fae283f\">>>", "siteName": "ballotpedia.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"872216792870fd9b\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Mathematics: State Achievement-Level Results\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"872216792870fd9b\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/achievement/?grade=8", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2dee5eea83ced91b\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nScroll down below the map to explore the percentage of students who performed at each of the NAEP mathematics achievement levels by state/jurisdiction in 2022.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2dee5eea83ced91b\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"80cbc2fb83e080c8\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nStates’ Demographically Adjusted Performance on the 2022 Nation’s Report Card\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"80cbc2fb83e080c8\">>>", "url": "https://www.urban.org/sites/default/files/2024-12/States_Demographically_Adjusted_Performance_on_the_2022_Nations_Report_Card.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"67b1d08e12480d6b\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTable 1 summarizes state rankings across the four NAEP tests in 2022. The top five states are · <strong>Massachusetts, Mississippi, Florida, Louisiana, and Texas</strong>.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"67b1d08e12480d6b\">>>", "siteName": "www.urban.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e06fd1b6f0c5ec30\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Mathematics: State Student Group Scores\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e06fd1b6f0c5ec30\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/groups/?grade=8", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"052e018df22f89f5\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nWhile average scores decreased between 2019 and 2022 for almost all student groups nationally, this overall pattern differed across the states. Compared to 2019, female students scored lower in 38 states in 2022, whereas male fourth-graders scored lower in 26 states.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"052e018df22f89f5\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ee9da807631b4a14\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Report Card: 2022 NAEP Mathematics Assessment\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ee9da807631b4a14\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/highlights/mathematics/2022/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6baebea052636767\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nResults are also available for the 50 states, the District of Columbia, Puerto Rico, and 26 participating districts. Students’ academic achievement during the COVID-19 pandemic is compared to pre-pandemic performance on the 2019 NAEP mathematics assessment as well as to previous mathematics assessments dating back to 1990.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6baebea052636767\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9c04d7ef6d222129\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT NATION  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9c04d7ef6d222129\">>>", "url": "https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011NP8.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"994ed8ebf5969793\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT · NATION  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"994ed8ebf5969793\">>>", "siteName": "nces.ed.gov"}]}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1775299991999}}
