{"type": "message", "id": "6a0241b1", "parentId": "6eaf99f7", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T10:53:37.119Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_93bb270a35ff4839bc5a3743", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"NAEP 2022 8th grade mathematics state scores table all 50 states\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 906,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c56708dced9db95e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: State Average Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c56708dced9db95e\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/scores/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5b14a90679e739a6\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe table below shows the number of states/jurisdictions with score increases or decreases in 2022 and how many states/jurisdictions scored higher, lower, or not significantly different than the nation (public) in NAEP mathematics.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5b14a90679e739a6\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e8a0b4eb88cb886a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT NATION  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e8a0b4eb88cb886a\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011NP8.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"200e341c7ec08429\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNOTE: <strong>The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from 0 to 500</strong>. Results presented in this report are based on public school students only.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"200e341c7ec08429\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a3346af84bf4a196\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: State Student Group Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a3346af84bf4a196\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/groups/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"618ed1591b8847bb\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWhile average scores decreased between 2019 and 2022 for almost all student groups nationally, this overall pattern differed across the states. Compared to 2019, <strong>female students scored lower in 38 states in 2022, whereas male fourth-graders scored lower in 26 states</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"618ed1591b8847bb\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"493868300731a7de\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 National Assessment of Educational Progress Grade 8 Mathematics Results\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"493868300731a7de\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.fldoe.org/core/fileparse.php/7667/urlt/2022NAEPGrade8Math.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4809e81dd9f99d56\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nFlorida NAEP Results Summary ....................................................................................4\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4809e81dd9f99d56\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.fldoe.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a6e98e60585f7de4\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP scores by state - Ballotpedia\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a6e98e60585f7de4\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ballotpedia.org/NAEP_scores_by_state\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bf871223585f1c1b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe table below details math and reading scores for students in fourth grade and eighth grade using the National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP). All 50 states and Washington, D.C.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bf871223585f1c1b\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ballotpedia.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8aac8f0d7da6374a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe Nation's Report Card | NAEP\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8aac8f0d7da6374a\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4d70316e784baf9b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nExplore NAEP results about student performance, and access state and district results, the NAEP data explorer, assessment items, item maps, and more.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4d70316e784baf9b\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"February 9, 2026\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b9d5434bfe6b27d4\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nExplore Results for the 2022 NAEP Mathematics Assessment\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b9d5434bfe6b27d4\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3a0a72e56f2d688a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nDownload a summary of the 2022 mathematics results. ... More detailed mathematics assessment results are available throughout this Report Card. ... The NAEP mathematics assessment measures students&#x27; knowledge and skills in mathematics and students&#x27; ability to apply their knowledge in problem-solving situations.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3a0a72e56f2d688a\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n