{"type": "message", "id": "86b6604a", "parentId": "0c1e9dce", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T10:54:09.520Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_19e80c28d7bd4f14aca1daa2", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"NAEP 2022 state rankings 8th grade mathematics all states scores list\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 919,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7d3e76af46c5d93f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: State Average Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7d3e76af46c5d93f\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/scores/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"22c71756c71fea94\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe table below shows the number of states/jurisdictions with score increases or decreases in 2022 and how many states/jurisdictions scored higher, lower, or not significantly different than the nation (public) in NAEP mathematics.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"22c71756c71fea94\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"85918a1a21930794\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nStates With the Highest NAEP Math Scores | U.S. News Best States\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"85918a1a21930794\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.usnews.com/news/best-states/rankings/education/prek-12/naep-math-scores\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8e69dae381a269f7\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nU.S. News ranks states based on NAEP math scores. See which states&#x27; eighth-graders are the best at math.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8e69dae381a269f7\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.usnews.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d95e4eb49e451ded\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: State Student Group Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d95e4eb49e451ded\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/groups/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d1fe9d38300dc0ef\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWhile average scores decreased between 2019 and 2022 for almost all student groups nationally, this overall pattern differed across the states. Compared to 2019, <strong>female students scored lower in 38 states in 2022, whereas male fourth-graders scored lower in 26 states</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d1fe9d38300dc0ef\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"be5686cac06969b9\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP State and District Snapshots\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"be5686cac06969b9\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/snapshots/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a690a1543b895351\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nExplore and download state and district snapshots of NAEP data in mathematics, reading, science, and writing.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a690a1543b895351\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4c332f07b6f80f05\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT NATION  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4c332f07b6f80f05\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011NP8.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a4b8cc24b0c37616\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP ACHIEVEMENT-LEVEL PERCENTAGES AND AVERAGE SCORE\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a4b8cc24b0c37616\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e30657b84bdc15cc\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP scores by state - Ballotpedia\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e30657b84bdc15cc\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ballotpedia.org/NAEP_scores_by_state\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1fe1eaefccf896d6\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe table below details math and reading scores for students in fourth grade and eighth grade using the National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP). All 50 states and Washington, D.C.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1fe1eaefccf896d6\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ballotpedia.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"910eceb58a51b6f3\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP State Results\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"910eceb58a51b6f3\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/state/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cb5e005fd3a793f4\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nResults are available for grades 4 and 8. View reading trends 2024 Mathematics Performance Trends for States and Districts Explore mathematics score trends and achievement-level results for individual states/jurisdictions. Results are available for grades 4 and 8. View math trends A look at how 2021-2022 state proficiency standards map onto NAEP Scales Read Mapping State Proficiency Standards Onto the NAEP Scales, the go-to study for comparing what states across the country expect from their students (i.e., their standards for proficient performance).\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cb5e005fd3a793f4\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2a8ce208163550af\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 NAEP Mathematics Assessment: Highlighted Results at Grades 4 and 8 for the Nation, States, and Districts | IES\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2a8ce208163550af\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/use-work/resource-library/report/statistical-analysis-report/2022-naep-mathematics-assessment-highlighted-results-grades-4-and-8-nation-states-and-districts\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cafb58a2b9ee2ee6\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThis report presents selected results from the National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP) 2022 mathematics assessment. The report includes national, state, and district results on the performance of fourth- and eighth-grade students. Results are presented in terms of average scores and as percentages of students performing at or above the three NAEP achievement levels: NAEP Basic, NAEP Proficient, and NAEP Advanced.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cafb58a2b9ee2ee6\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5ffef0e2e64d4553\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nhttps://cde.state.co.us/assessment/sof2022naepmath...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5ffef0e2e64d4553\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.cde.state.co.us/assessment/sof2022naepmathgrades4and8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5a2353ad4b5ae79d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nPK\\u0003\\u0004\\u0014\\u0000\\u0006\\u0000\\b\\u0000\\u0000\\u0000!\\u0000΁J\\u0001\\u0000\\u0000\\b\\u0000\\u0000\\u0013\\u0000\\b\\u0002[Content_Types].xml \\u0004\\u0002(\\u0000\\u0002\\u0000\\u0000\\u0000\\u0000\\u0000\\u0000\\u0000\\u0000\\u0000\\u0000\\u0000\\u0000\\u0000\\u0000\\u0000\\u0000\\u0000\\u0000\\u0000\\u0000\\u0000\\u0000\\u0000\\u0000\\u0000\\u0000