ore declines, <strong>18 scored lower than the national average score for public school students in 2022; 16 had average scores that were not significantly different from the national public average; and 17 scored higher</strong>. Explore detailed state average score results ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d2063e407b0611ff\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b3145e197e077a5f\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nAnalysis of 2022 NAEP Mathematics and Reading Results\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b3145e197e077a5f\">>>", "url": "https://whiteboardadvisors.com/analysis-of-2022-naep-mathematics-and-reading-results/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"195672ce87d16395\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n<strong>Average eighth grade math score fell from 282 in 2019 to 274 in 2022</strong> – a decline of 8 points · 38% of eighth-graders performed below NAEP Basic, compared to 31% in 2019\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"195672ce87d16395\">>>", "published": "October 24, 2022", "siteName": "whiteboardadvisors.com"}]}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1775300061305}}
