{"type": "message", "id": "4d86cda8", "parentId": "b97c87e8", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T10:56:33.265Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_57e01350a3b94fd0afc9554b", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"Arizona NAEP 2022 8th grade mathematics score news article October 2022\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 936,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6d1b7f1378a61504\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT ARIZONA  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6d1b7f1378a61504\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011AZ8.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"887a83c4bcb7c0d0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNOTE: <strong>The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from 0 to 500</strong>. Results presented in this report are based on public school students only.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"887a83c4bcb7c0d0\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"dd811cb5d2f38fc2\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNational academic progress report is out - See how AZ students performed - Children's Action Alliance\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"dd811cb5d2f38fc2\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://azchildren.org/news-and-events/the-2022-naep-scores-are-out/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"968a5a41ddb16a2e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIt was administered in 2019, and it shows how students performed before and after the COVID pandemic · Although scores in math have consistently increased since 1990, average mathematics scores for the nation in 2022 were lower by 5 points at the fourth-grade level and <strong>8 points</strong> at the eighth-grade ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"968a5a41ddb16a2e\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"November 2, 2022\",\n      \"siteName\": \"azchildren.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ca6ee2c6bcc899c5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: State Average Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ca6ee2c6bcc899c5\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/scores/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2e91baa08bcfdfda\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTo compare average mathematics scores between states/jurisdictions and the nation (public), use the NAEP State Profiles Tool. ... In the 43 states/jurisdictions where scores were lower in 2022 than 2019, <strong>the size of the score differences ranged from 2 to 14 points</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2e91baa08bcfdfda\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e174e2da438df12d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Report Card: 2022 NAEP Mathematics Assessment\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e174e2da438df12d\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/highlights/mathematics/2022/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ab260c2075f77273\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIn 2022, the average fourth-grade mathematics score decreased by 5 points and was lower than all previous assessment years going back to 2005; the average score was one point higher compared to 2003. <strong>The average eighth-grade mathematics score decreased by 8 points compared to 2019 and was lower</strong> ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ab260c2075f77273\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteNam